  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"In 1968-69, I was keeping some notes, on location. A year or so later, I was talking with Frederick Ted Castle and Leandro Katz, who were publishing under the name TVRT (The Vanishing Rotating Triangle). They wanted to see those notes and asked if they could publish them! I responded okay let's. Hence Notes on Location followed shortly thereafter by Notes on Location II ... There are more notes in the drawer."--Peter Downbrough, March 28, 2012.</subfield>
